 The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each holds, listed a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty is shown as having none rather than left blank `[REQ-VET-001]`.
 
+The directory is served both as the page a reader browses and as a machine-readable rendering of the same veterinarians at a second route. That second route is a supported surface `[REQ-VET-003]`. Either surface can be narrowed to a single specialty. When a specialty is named, only the veterinarians holding it are listed; when none is named, both surfaces behave as they did before. A specialty is matched by its whole name, disregarding letter case — a partial name does not match. A specialty that no veterinarian holds yields an empty list under a normal successful response rather than an error. This includes a name outside the clinic's specialties entirely. A specialty that is empty or only spaces is treated as though none were named, mirroring an empty owner search. The narrowing is requested by naming the specialty on the request rather than through any control on the page. The page's own filtered listing is shown a page at a time, and pagination links carry the chosen specialty so a filtered result stays navigable. The narrowing uses a specialty the directory already displays; no free-text veterinarian search is added `[REQ-VET-003]`.
+
 **Done when:**
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given the clinic's veterinarians, when the directory is opened, then each name and its specialties are listed a page at a time.
