+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty that veterinarians hold, when either surface is requested with that specialty, then only the veterinarians holding it are listed.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty differing from a held specialty only by letter case, when either surface is filtered, then it matches.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given only part of a specialty's name, when either surface is filtered, then it does not match.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty no veterinarian holds, when either surface is filtered, then an empty veterinarian list is returned under a successful response, not an error.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty that is empty or only spaces, when either surface is filtered, then the result is the same as requesting the surface with no specialty.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given no specialty, when either surface is requested, then it behaves as it did before this capability.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a filtered directory page, when a link to another page of the filtered result is followed, then the chosen specialty is kept and the next page stays filtered.
 
